<title>SOUTH AFRICA: De Beers year shr, div jumps.</title>
<headline>De Beers year shr, div jumps.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31</p>
<p>			(million U.S. dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>Earnings per linked unit excluding</p>
<p>    retained associates (U.S. cts)   218    vs 164.0</p>
<p>Earnings per linked unit including</p>
<p>    retained associates (U.S. cts)   354    vs 259.0</p>
<p>Div (U.S. cts)			     102.7  +10.5 percent</p>
<p>Div (S.Africa cts)			 480.7  vs 339.1</p>
<p>Attrib income excluding</p>
<p>    retained associates		  828    vs 624.0</p>
<p>Attrib income including</p>
<p>    retained associates		1,344    vs 986</p>
<p>Combined diamond account		 803    vs 760</p>
<p>Full name: De Beers Consolidated Mines Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters had forecast rand earnings of 1,301 cents, with the range 1,197-1,400, and dividend of 415.4, with the range 370-447.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
